                                        "entry_id": "99bfa59b-e52c-3bc3-b82f-af0006fa6d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being known a priori"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5553523-561e-4f41-bf1e-9f2f32607aa3",
                                                "sense_id": "53702539-04b3-3a7a-8b03-204303ad6580",
                                                "text": "The apriority is, however, not to be merely as a result of the fixing of the meaning of the term, such as when I dub my cat ‘Cat’ and then claim to know a priori that my cat is called ‘Cat’."
